  "summary": "A liquid ring vacuum pump has a bladed impeller mounted off-centre in a round casing partly filled with liquid (usually water). As it turns, the liquid is thrown out to form a ring concentric with the casing. Because the impeller is eccentric, the spaces between blades grow (drawing gas in through the suction port) and then shrink (compressing it out through the discharge port). It tolerates wet, dirty and condensable gases.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive-displacement vacuum pump / compressor",
    "type": "Liquid ring, single stage, flat port plate"
  },
